  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rural Water Points Project in Fromager and Savannah Regions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims at drilling 800 productive boreholes and equipping 1,000 pumps in order to secure 15_20 liters per capita per day potable
water to the population of some villages in the Fromager and Savannah regions and to raise the average coverage of rural water points from 61% to 86% and from 54% to 84% respectively in the Fromager and Savannah.</narrative>
  </description>
